  bootwright / controller uninstall
      Remove, on a host that holds no context and no installer media, the host packages
      controller install recorded as its own, through the host's own dnf, then every root
      Bootwright keeps on this host, whole: the store /var/lib/bootwright, the staging
      directory /var/lib/bootwright-staging, the log root /var/log/bootwright, the hosted root
      /var/lib/bootwright-hosted with any physical-erase receipts, and the libvirt image prefix
      /var/lib/libvirt/images/bootwright when it is empty. It never removes a package present
      before Bootwright, a package a controller stage installed, this executable, or what a
      context realized on an SSH placement host. It refuses before any effect while a context
      or an image remains, naming the commands that remove each, while any libvirt domain,
      network or pool, systemd unit, quadlet source or podman container Bootwright owns
      remains, naming each, while another command holds the store, while guest disks remain
      under the libvirt image prefix, and, without --keep-packages, when the install record
      cannot say what install added or another installed package requires one of them.
      --discard-unreadable is the exit for a store this build cannot read, such as one an
      earlier build wrote, and for guest disks no removal took back: after the same proof that
      no owned object remains, it removes every root and the libvirt image prefix whole, and
      never a package. The plan shows dnf's own removal preview and what stays before
      confirmation. A host with nothing to remove prints Nothing to do. Review the plan before
      confirming; --yes skips ordinary confirmation.

  Usage
    bootwright controller uninstall [flags]

  Command flags
      --discard-unreadable  Discard what this build cannot read or attribute: a store another
                            build wrote, or guest disks no removal took back; never removes
                            packages
      --keep-packages       Leave every host package installed and remove only Bootwright's
                            state
      --yes                 Confirm the command's ordinary confirmation

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  Examples
    bootwright controller uninstall
